        "UPDATE: Based on your response, I’m even more relieved that I did not receive treatment there. You are a liar, a scammer, and you’re an ethical.\n\nI did not walk in cursing or behaving aggressively. I was upset because I had legitimate questions about my dental care, and your manager did not like being questioned. Judging by other reviews, I’m clearly not the only patient who has raised concerns about her attitude. I’m taking my information to the news.\n*****************\nMy experience at this office was horrible. I was upset because I was not screened properly. And drove all the way down there for absolutely nothing. I explained that I have resorption involving a tooth that has already had a root canal, yet the manager insisted this doctor could take care of it.\n\nTreatment for a complicated case like this may involve specialized endodontic procedures such as root canal retreatment or endodontic surgery, including an apicoectomy. I specifically questioned how they could offer that specialized treatment when the doctor is not an endodontist. She repeatedly insisted he could and told me, “I’ve been doing this for 20 years.” My response was simple: then you’ve been doing it wrong for 20 years, or you need to go back to school.\n\nThe situation became confrontational after I started questioning their ethics and whether I was being given accurate information. They told me they would not treat me.\n\nPatients have every right to ask questions before allowing someone to perform irreversible dental work. I’m very glad I asked mine.\n\nMy response was “You made me come down here for nothing.”\nThe manager said, “ I didn’t make you do anything “\nWow.\nHorrible response. Arrogance.\nThe manager is a reflection of the entire staff and office.",
